<!-- SYNTHETIC FIXTURE: NEGATIVE TWIN of synth-ubl-good-export_ubl.xml.
     Byte-for-byte identical to that clean export-outside-the-EU invoice EXCEPT
     the mandated exemption reason is stripped from the single G VAT breakdown:
     both the BT-121 exemption reason code (VATEX-EU-G) and the BT-120 exemption
     reason text are deleted.

     For an Export outside the EU (VAT category G) BR-G-10 mandates that a VAT
     breakdown (BG-23) carrying category code G SHALL have a VAT exemption
     reason code (BT-121) OR a VAT exemption reason text (BT-120). With BOTH
     gone that disjunction is broken, so the ONLY fired rule is BR-G-10 (fatal).
     The seller VAT id (BT-31, still present: DE000000000) keeps BR-G-02
     satisfied, every G line rate is still 0 (BR-G-05), the breakdown taxable
     still equals Σ G nets (BR-G-08) and its tax amount is still 0.00 (BR-G-09),
     and the arithmetic is untouched (VAT total 0.00, tax inclusive = tax
     exclusive = 11400.00 all still reconcile), so no BR-CO totals rule and no
     other BR-G rule fires. Exactly one distinct fatal, isolating the BR-G-10
     shape: valid=false, exit 1. -->
